CTA-Notes/Integration/12-graphql-api.content:
(Salesforce GraphQL API Developer Guide) (GraphQL API Overview)
What It Is

Query language and runtime for APIs — client specifies exactly what data it needs
Salesforce implementation allows querying sObjects and relationships in a single request
Returns only the requested fields — no over-fetching
Single endpoint: POST /services/data/vXX.X/graphql


Why GraphQL

























BenefitDetailNo over-fetchingClient requests only needed fields; reduces payload sizeNo under-fetchingSingle request can traverse relationships (Account → Contacts → Cases)Strongly typedSchema enforced; better developer tooling and introspectionGreat for mobileReduced data transfer; single round-trip for complex data needs

Core Concepts
Query Syntax
query {
  uiapi {
    query {
      Account(
        where: { Name: { like: &quot;Acme%&quot; } }
        first: 10
      ) {
        edges {
          node {
            Id
            Name { value }
            Contacts {
              edges {
                node {
                  Id
                  LastName { value }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

Wraps SOQL semantics in a graph traversal model
edges / node pattern is standard GraphQL pagination (Relay-style)
first, last, after, before for pagination

Mutations (DML)
mutation {
  uiapi {
    AccountCreate(input: {
      record: { Name: &quot;New Corp&quot; }
    }) {
      Record {
        Id
        Name { value }
      }
    }
  }
}
Supports: Create, Update, Delete mutations on sObjects.
Type System and Introspection

Schema is auto-generated from the org’s metadata
Use introspection (__schema, __type) to explore available objects and fields in tooling
Strongly typed — field types match Salesforce field metadata


GraphQL vs REST API













































REST APIGraphQL APIEndpointPer-resource URLsSingle endpointResponse shapeFixed by serverDefined by clientMultiple objectsMultiple calls or CompositeSingle query with traversalOver-fetchingCommonEliminatedLearning curveLowModerateMobile suitabilityGoodExcellentMaturity in SalesforceVery matureNewer (GA in API v55.0+)



                  CTA positioning 



GraphQL is the right choice when the client is a mobile app or a custom UI that needs flexible, relationship-rich queries without multiple round-trips. For server-to-server integrations, REST or Bulk API is usually simpler.



Pagination

Relay-style cursor pagination via edges / node / pageInfo
pageInfo.hasNextPage and pageInfo.endCursor for forward pagination
Use first: N after: &quot;&lt;cursor&gt;&quot; to page through results


Authentication

Same OAuth 2.0 flows as REST API
Bearer token in Authorization header


Key Limits





















LimitValueMax query depth10 levelsMax records per query2,000 (same as REST)API request limitsShared with REST API daily limit

Related Notes

REST API — REST API for comparison
UI API — UI API also serves mobile/web; complementary
Composite API — alternative for multiple REST operations in one call
